WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:04.673
- [Voiceover] In 1992, Nickelodeon
debuted the TV show Guts.

00:00:04.673 --> 00:00:06.608
It was just like American Gladiator,

00:00:06.608 --> 00:00:09.057
only the contestants were all kids.

00:00:09.057 --> 00:00:10.296
- [Voiceover] The rocks have tumbled,

00:00:10.296 --> 00:00:12.393
the smoke is smokin'.

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:14.898
- [Voiceover] And while the
show was epic in every way,

00:00:14.898 --> 00:00:17.479
the theme song is one of
those pieces where you start

00:00:17.479 --> 00:00:21.449
singing it and somebody
next to you joins in.

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:23.119
So we found the guy who wrote it.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:25.409
- My name's Rick Witkowski
and I am the composer

00:00:25.409 --> 00:00:29.230
of the Nickelodeon theme song, Guts.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.070
♫ Do you have it,

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.489
♫ Do do do you have it

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:32.322
♫ Guts

00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:34.919
♫ Do do

00:00:34.919 --> 00:00:36.161
♫ Do do you have it

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:36.994
♫ Guts.

00:00:36.994 --> 00:00:37.827
♫ It takes deep dedication♫

00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:40.246
When I got the call to do this piece,

00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:41.649
hip hop was just coming of age.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:43.899
Immediately it came to mind

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:46.319
that do do do do you have it, Guts.

00:00:46.319 --> 00:00:48.007
They liked it and they said you think

00:00:48.007 --> 00:00:50.199
you can put a little rap to it?

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:53.641
I said sure, I'm a Polish
guy from West Virginia.

00:00:53.641 --> 00:00:55.561
I can rap, yeah.

00:00:55.561 --> 00:00:56.499
♫ It takes a certain kind of something

00:00:56.499 --> 00:00:57.689
♫ To keep the heart pumping

00:00:57.689 --> 00:00:59.219
♫ Something everybody needs to achieve

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:01.459
♫ To succeed, you'll need a lot.♫

00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:03.409
A lot of words, a lot of words.

00:01:03.409 --> 00:01:04.899
♫ Do you have it, Guts.♫

00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:07.067
They were big on the sound
effect stuff in that tune.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.396
You can hear me in there, eww, ahh, ahh.

00:01:10.396 --> 00:01:11.699
Aggro crag.

00:01:11.699 --> 00:01:13.626
I sampled myself.

00:01:13.626 --> 00:01:15.169
- [Voiceover] So Rick,
he didn't just write

00:01:15.169 --> 00:01:16.667
the theme song for Guts,

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:20.387
he was kind of the 90s
jingle guy for Nickelodeon.

00:01:20.387 --> 00:01:23.329
- Guts was my first, you know,
first show for Nickelodeon.

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:25.418
I did some music for The Big Help.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.278
(guitar music)

00:01:27.278 --> 00:01:29.307
Did all the music for
Kids’ Choice Awards.

00:01:29.307 --> 00:01:31.017
♫ Kids’ Choice ♫

00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:32.926
Figure It Out.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.963
The remake of Family Double Dare.

00:01:34.963 --> 00:01:37.614
- [Voiceover] Double Dare 2000.

00:01:37.614 --> 00:01:38.995
- I did stuff for Nick at Nite also.

00:01:38.995 --> 00:01:40.634
♫ Nick at Nite

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:42.835
♫ The place for TV hits♫

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.854
Oh but here's a show
that I forgot to mention.

00:01:44.854 --> 00:01:47.745
I did the music for a show
called Action League Now.

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:49.915
- [Voiceover] Action League Now,

00:01:49.915 --> 00:01:51.415
starring The Flesh.

00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:56.534
- On my bucket list I, you know,

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:59.553
would love to be involved in
having a hit record, you know?

00:01:59.553 --> 00:02:03.294
I'm still working on that, but
I guess you know to a degree,

00:02:03.294 --> 00:02:05.833
like, the Guts theme, it’s my hit.

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:07.679
So I'm pretty happy about that.

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:09.551
♫ Do, do, do you have it?

00:02:09.551 --> 00:02:13.051
♫ Guts♫

